  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $59.8M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The agency executed 400 awards with an average award size of $150K, and obligations fell 99.8% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show much larger totals in prior years: FY22 and FY23 each had $33.4B, FY24 had $29.9B, FY25 had $21.3B, and FY26 had $24.9B. The FY2027 to date total concentrates in a few categories and vendors. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounts for $23.8M of FY2027 to date obligations, while Custom Computer Programming Services accounts for $18M. AMERICAN TYPE CULTURE COLLECTION received $23.5M, and PERATON INC. received $18.7M among the top vendors. The mix shows a strong tilt toward R&D and IT services in the partial fiscal year, with several health services and consulting categories also represented among smaller amounts.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why are FY2027 obligations so much lower than prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $59.8M in FY2027 to date, compared with $24.9B in FY26 and higher totals in earlier years. Obligations fell 99.8% year over year, reflecting that current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). The disparity with FY22 through FY26 shows the FY2027 figure is not a full-year total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which categories and vendors account for most FY2027 spending?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $23.8M of FY2027 to date obligations, and Custom Computer Programming Services accounted for $18M. AMERICAN TYPE CULTURE COLLECTION received $23.5M and PERATON INC. received $18.7M, making them the two largest vendors in the partial year. Other notable categories include Facilities Support Services at $10.7M and Offices of Physicians, Mental Health Specialists at $5M."
      }
    ]
  },
