    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Health and Human Services spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $59.8M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The agency executed 400 awards with an average award size of $150K. Prior fiscal years were much larger: FY22 and FY23 had $33.4B each, FY24 had $29.9B, FY25 had $21.3B, and FY26 had $24.9B, and obligations fell 99.8% year over year."
